{"id":"SMA-515","title":"RunInterrupt ergonomics: add terminal_event() and From<RunInterrupt> for RunError","description":"## Background

Follow-up from <issue id="2ac68c98-be9c-4cfc-bfab-2ec8f778dc5f" href="https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-422/hoist-the-terminal-vs-cancel-precedence-resolver-into-core-for-durable">SMA-422</issue> (PR #193), which hoisted the terminal-vs-cancel precedence rule into `paigasus-helikon-core` as `AgentEvent::is_terminal()`, `RunInterrupt { Cancelled, TimedOut }` with `run_error()` / `terminal_message()`, and `effective_interrupt(interrupt, saw_terminal)`.

Two small additive gaps were noted during the final whole-branch review and deliberately deferred — both are non-breaking and can land any time.

## 1. `RunInterrupt::terminal_event()`

Constructing the synthesized terminal frame is still hand-rolled in every runner:

```rust
AgentEvent::RunFailed { error: i.terminal_message().to_owned() }
```

That appears in `runtime-tokio/src/lib.rs` (`run_streamed`) and, in spirit, in `runtime-temporal/src/runner.rs`. A `terminal_event(self) -> AgentEvent` would move the last hand-rolled piece into core, so a runner never assembles the frame itself:

```rust
impl RunInterrupt {
    /// The terminal event a streaming runner yields when this interrupt wins.
    pub fn terminal_event(self) -> AgentEvent {
        AgentEvent::RunFailed { error: self.terminal_message().to_owned() }
    }
}
```

## 2. `impl From<RunInterrupt> for RunError`

`run_error()` already exists and is the canonical mapping. A `From` impl alongside it is idiomatic and makes `?`/`.into()` call sites read naturally. Keep `run_error()` — it is the documented name and `From` should delegate to it, not duplicate the match.

## Notes

* Both are **purely additive**, so release-plz will treat them as a patch bump on `paigasus-helikon-core` and no breaking-change ritual is needed.
* Add both to the existing `interrupt_tests` module in `crates/paigasus-helikon-core/src/runner.rs`, and assert `terminal_event()` agrees with `terminal_message()` rather than restating the literals.
* Migrate the tokio call site in the same PR, otherwise the helper ships with no consumer.
* Low priority: this is ergonomics, not correctness. The rule itself is already single-homed and tested.","projectMilestone":{"id":"5060a2bb-a702-4bcf-9a8e-75193e0cc29a","name":"Runtimes, Providers & Evals"},"priority":{"value":4,"name":"Low"},"url":"https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-515/runinterrupt-ergonomics-add-terminal-event-and-fromruninterrupt-for","gitBranchName":"feature/sma-515-runinterrupt-ergonomics-add-terminal_event-and","createdAt":"2026-08-14T05:46:46.294Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T05:46:46.294Z","archivedAt":null,"completedAt":null,"startedAt":null,"canceledAt":null,"dueDate":null,"slaStartedAt":null,"slaMediumRiskAt":null,"slaHighRiskAt":null,"slaBreachesAt":null,"status":"Backlog","statusType":"backlog","labels":["area:core","stage:3","Improvement"],"attachments":[],"documents":[],"stateHistory":[{"state":{"id":"46bb932e-d4b2-4e1a-8a2a-48ca21321735","name":"Backlog","type":"backlog"},"startedAt":"2026-08-14T05:46:46.294Z","endedAt":null}],"createdBy":"Sven Maschek","createdById":"ba6021cb-56c5-43aa-9797-fab3599d7ead","project":"Paigasus Helikon","projectId":"5d1fd72d-af2d-40f5-b562-fa04f8018610","team":"Sven Maschek","teamId":"7178572e-d61f-4cf0-bbcb-4e03c8d9f39e","relations":{"blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"relatedTo":[{"id":"SMA-516","title":"runtime-temporal: cover run_streamed's terminal synthesis with a runner-level test"},{"id":"SMA-422","title":"Hoist the terminal-vs-cancel precedence resolver into core for durable runners"}],"duplicateOf":null}}

